truct the surface development of the square pipe. (15 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-09 04:28:01','2026-08-09 04:28:01'),(91,4,5,'SECTION C',5,'Question 5',NULL,15,'(15 marks)','The plan and elevation of two straight lines are shown in figure 5. Construct and state:\n (i) the true length of the lines; (mark the true lengths as (A, B and C)\n (ii) the true angle between them;\n (iii) the distance between A and C.','5. The plan and elevation of two straight lines are shown in figure 5. Construct and state:\n (i) the true length of the lines; (mark the true lengths as (A, B and C)\n (ii) the true angle between them;\n (iii) the distance between A and C. (15 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-09 04:28:01','2026-08-09 04:28:01'),(92,4,6,'SECTION C',6,'Question 6',NULL,15,'(15 marks)','Two views of a double-ended bearing housing are shown in figure 6. Draw the bearing in isometric projection with corner X the lowest.','6. Two views of a double-ended bearing housing are shown in figure 6. Draw the bearing in isometric projection with corner X the lowest. (15 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-09 04:28:01','2026-08-09 04:28:01'),(93,4,7,'SECTION C',7,'Question 7',NULL,15,'(15 marks)','Sketch the following tools:\n (i) mallet;\n (ii) flat screw driver;\n (iii) centre punch.','7. Sketch the following tools:\n (i) mallet;\n (ii) flat screw driver;\n (iii) centre punch. (15 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-09 04:28:02','2026-08-09 04:28:02'),(94,5,1,'SECTION A',1,'Question 1','1(a)',4,'(4 marks)','Given the matrices A = [−1 2 \\n 2 −1 \\n 3 4] and B = [1 −2 3 \\n 6 −1 2] determine (AB)^','1. (a) Given the matrices A = [−1 2 \\n 2 −1 \\n 3 4] and B = [1 −2 3 \\n 6 −1 2] determine (AB)^(4 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:38','2026-08-10 19:55:38'),(95,5,2,'SECTION A',1,'Question 1','1(b)',6,'(6 marks)','Find the inverse of the matrix A = [1 2 4 \\n 4 1 3 \\n 2 1 1].','1. (b) Find the inverse of the matrix A = [1 2 4 \\n 4 1 3 \\n 2 1 1]. (6 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:39','2026-08-10 19:55:39'),(96,5,3,'SECTION A',1,'Question 1','1(c)',10,'(10 marks)','Three forces F₁, F₂, and F₃, acting at a point in a mechanical system satisfy the simultaneous equations: F₁ + F₂ + F₃ = 9 F₁ − 2F₂ + 2F₃ = 7 3F₁ + F₂ + F₃ = 15 Use Cramer’s rule to determine the values of the forces.','1. (c) Three forces F₁, F₂, and F₃, acting at a point in a mechanical system satisfy the simultaneous equations: F₁ + F₂ + F₃ = 9 F₁ − 2F₂ + 2F₃ = 7 3F₁ + F₂ + F₃ = 15 Use Cramer’s rule to determine the values of the forces. (10 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:39','2026-08-10 19:55:39'),(97,5,4,'SECTION A',2,'Question 2','2(a)',5,'(5 marks)','Write down the sixth term in the binomial expansion of (3x + 2y)¹⁰, and determine its value when x = 1/2 and y = 1/3.','2. (a) Write down the sixth term in the binomial expansion of (3x + 2y)¹⁰, and determine its value when x = 1/2 and y = 1/3. (5 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:39','2026-08-10 19:55:39'),(98,5,5,'SECTION A',2,'Question 2','2(b)',4,'(4 marks)','Use the binomial theorem to find the value of 1/√1.01, correct to six decimal places.','2. (b) Use the binomial theorem to find the value of 1/√1.01, correct to six decimal places. (4 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:39','2026-08-10 19:55:39'),(99,5,6,'SECTION A',2,'Question 2','2(c)(i)',NULL,NULL,'Show that, for very small values of x, √(1+x)/(1-x) = 1 + x + 1/2 x².','2. (c) (i) Show that, for very small values of x, √(1+x)/(1-x) = 1 + x + 1/2 x².','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:39','2026-08-10 19:55:39'),(100,5,7,'SECTION A',2,'Question 2','2(c)(ii)',11,'(11 marks)','By setting x = 1/26 in question 2(c)(i) above, determine the value of √27, correct to four decimal places.','2. (c) (ii) By setting x = 1/26 in question 2(c)(i) above, determine the value of √27, correct to four decimal places. (11 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:39','2026-08-10 19:55:39'),(101,5,8,'SECTION A',3,'Question 3','3(a)(i)',NULL,NULL,'Show that sin 3θ = 3 sin θ − 4 sin³θ.','3. (a) (i) Show that sin 3θ = 3 sin θ − 4 sin³θ.','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:42','2026-08-10 19:55:42'),(102,5,9,'SECTION A',3,'Question 3','3(a)(ii)',9,'(9 marks)','By setting θ = π/3 in (i) above, determine the value of sin(π/3) without using a calculator or tables. Leave surds in the answer.','3. (a) (ii) By setting θ = π/3 in (i) above, determine the value of sin(π/3) without using a calculator or tables. Leave surds in the answer. (9 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:43','2026-08-10 19:55:43'),(103,5,10,'SECTION A',3,'Question 3','3(b)(i)',NULL,NULL,'Prove the identities: (i) (cos B − cos C)/(sin C − sin B) = −tan (B + C)/2.','3. (b) Prove the identities: (i) (cos B − cos C)/(sin C − sin B) = −tan (B + C)/2.','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:43','2026-08-10 19:55:43'),(104,5,11,'SECTION A',3,'Question 3','3(b)(ii)',6,'(6 marks)','1 + cos θ/sin θ + sin θ/1 + cos θ = 2 cosec θ.','3. (b) (ii) 1 + cos θ/sin θ + sin θ/1 + cos θ = 2 cosec θ. (6 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:43','2026-08-10 19:55:43'),(105,5,12,'SECTION A',3,'Question 3','3(c)',5,'(5 marks)','Solve the equation: sin x + sin 3x + sin 5x = 0, for values of x between 0° and 180° inclusive.','3. (c) Solve the equation: sin x + sin 3x + sin 5x = 0, for values of x between 0° and 180° inclusive. (5 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:43','2026-08-10 19:55:43'),(106,5,13,'SECTION A',4,'Question 4','4(a)',5,'(5 marks)','Given that y = 1/(x + 2), find dy/dx from first principles.','4. (a) Given that y = 1/(x + 2), find dy/dx from first principles. (5 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:44','2026-08-10 19:55:44'),(107,5,14,'SECTION A',4,'Question 4','4(b)',5,'(5 marks)','Find the first derivative of f(x) = cos(x + 1/(2−x)).','4. (b) Find the first derivative of f(x) = cos(x + 1/(2−x)). (5 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:44','2026-08-10 19:55:44'),(108,5,15,'SECTION A',4,'Question 4','4(c)',10,'(10 marks)','Find the stationary points of the function f(x) = x³ + 6x² + 9x − 8, and determine their nature.','4. (c) Find the stationary points of the function f(x) = x³ + 6x² + 9x − 8, and determine their nature. (10 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:44','2026-08-10 19:55:44'),(109,5,16,'SECTION A',5,'Question 5','5(a)(i)',3,'(3 marks)','Evaluate the integrals: ∫(from 0 to 5) (3 cos x + sin² x) dx.','5. (a) (i) Evaluate the integrals: ∫(from 0 to 5) (3 cos x + sin² x) dx. (3 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:44','2026-08-10 19:55:44'),(110,5,17,'SECTION A',5,'Question 5','5(a)(ii)',5,'(5 marks)','∫(from 0 to ∞) (x + x² + x³)/√x dx.','5. (a) (ii) ∫(from 0 to ∞) (x + x² + x³)/√x dx. (5 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:44','2026-08-10 19:55:44'),(111,5,18,'SECTION A',5,'Question 5','5(b)',4,'(4 marks)','Show that ∫(cot² θ) dθ = c − θ − cot θ, where c is an arbitrary constant of integration.','5. (b) Show that ∫(cot² θ) dθ = c − θ − cot θ, where c is an arbitrary constant of integration. (4 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:45','2026-08-10 19:55:45'),(112,5,19,'SECTION A',5,'Question 5','5(c)',8,'(8 marks)','Sketch the region bounded by the straight lines x = 0, x = y and y = 1, and use integration to find the area of the region.','5. (c) Sketch the region bounded by the straight lines x = 0, x = y and y = 1, and use integration to find the area of the region. (8 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:45','2026-08-10 19:55:45'),(113,5,20,'SECTION A',6,'Question 6','6(a)',4,'(4 marks)','Find the angle between the vectors A = 3i − 2j + 5k and B = 4i − 7j + 8k.','6. (a) Find the angle between the vectors A = 3i − 2j + 5k and B = 4i − 7j + 8k. (4 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:45','2026-08-10 19:55:45'),(114,5,21,'SECTION A',6,'Question 6','6(b)',5,'(5 marks)','Determine the value of the constant a if the three vectors A = 2i − j + ak, B = −2i − 2j and C = 4i + 2j − 3k are coplanar.','6. (b) Determine the value of the constant a if the three vectors A = 2i − j + ak, B = −2i − 2j and C = 4i + 2j − 3k are coplanar. (5 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:45','2026-08-10 19:55:45'),(115,5,22,'SECTION A',6,'Question 6','6(c)',11,'(11 marks)','Temperature distribution in a factory is given by the scalar function T = 2x²y + 3xz. Determine, at the point (1, 3, −2), (i) grad T (ii) curl grad T (iii) div grad T.','6. (c) Temperature distribution in a factory is given by the scalar function T = 2x²y + 3xz. Determine, at the point (1, 3, −2), (i) grad T (ii) curl grad T (iii) div grad T. (11 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:46','2026-08-10 19:55:46'),(116,5,23,'SECTION A',7,'Question 7','7(a)',5,'(5 marks)','Solve the equation 8x² + 9x + 1 = 0, by factorisation.','7. (a) Solve the equation 8x² + 9x + 1 = 0, by factorisation. (5 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:46','2026-08-10 19:55:46'),(117,5,24,'SECTION A',7,'Question 7','7(b)',7,'(7 marks)','By completing the square, determine the constants p, q and r such that 4x² + 7x + 6 = p(x + q)² + r.','7. (b) By completing the square, determine the constants p, q and r such that 4x² + 7x + 6 = p(x + q)² + r. (7 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:46','2026-08-10 19:55:46'),(118,5,25,'SECTION A',7,'Question 7','7(c)',8,'(8 marks)','Solve the equation x + 5 − 1/(x + 4) = 1.','7. (c) Solve the equation x + 5 − 1/(x + 4) = 1. (8 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:46','2026-08-10 19:55:46'),(119,5,26,'SECTION A',8,'Question 8','8(a)',5,'(5 marks)','Given that u = 1 − 2xy − x² + y², show that du/dx and d²u/dy² = 0.','8. (a) Given that u = 1 − 2xy − x² + y², show that du/dx and d²u/dy² = 0. (5 marks)','{\"source\": \"openai\"}','2026-08-10 19:55:46'